{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfcSHrhaRaKDLbpsxmE32", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I compared the barcode against all ten videos. For each video I sampled the average frame color once per second, stretched that sequence to the barcode's width, and measured the color difference stripe by stripe.\n\n| Video | Mean per-stripe color difference (lower is better) |\n|---|---|\n| **G \u2013 Yes Yes Vegetables Song** | **18.9** |\n| A \u2013 Johny Johny Yes Papa | 23.8 |\n| B \u2013 Wheels on the Bus | 32.1 |\n| D \u2013 Baa Baa Black Sheep | 33.9 |\n| All others (C, E, F, H, I, J) | 41.6 or higher |\n\nG matches best, with A a fairly close second. A's overall average color is actually a little closer to the barcode's (12.3 vs 16.1). But G follows the barcode's left-to-right sequence of colors more closely, which matters more for this question. I didn't try shifting the alignment, so G is my best guess rather than a certain match.\n\nAnswer: G"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 944, "cache_read_input_tokens": 6505, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 944}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "694654a5-1e8c-4dd5-ad4f-c267dcf6bbd5", "uuid": "ee7a3238-d041-43bd-b513-2c580a1b3e80", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T00:07:57.159Z", "request_id": "req_011CfcSHrMEktka39fdUUKXH"}
